![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Improve the robustness of the staleness check. If the owner file is missing or corrupt (e.g., if a process was killed between `mkdirSync` and `writeFileSync`), the current logic returns `false`, causing all other workers to wait for the full 30s timeout. Checking the directory's modification time provides a reliable fallback. Additionally, `process.kill(pid, 0)` should specifically check for `ESRCH` to determine if a process is gone, as it may throw `EPERM` if the process exists but belongs to another user.

```javascript
function _isInitLockStale(ownerFile, staleMs) {
  try {
    const { pid, ts } = JSON.parse(readFileSync(ownerFile, "utf-8"));
    const processGone = (() => {
      try {
        process.kill(pid, 0);
        return false;
      } catch (e) {
        return e.code === "ESRCH";
      }
    })();
    return processGone || (Date.now() - ts > staleMs);
  } catch {
    try {
      const stats = statSync(dirname(ownerFile));
      return (Date.now() - stats.mtimeMs) > staleMs;
    } catch {
      return false;
    }
  }
}
```

